# =============================================================================
# Runtime state — regenerated on every run, never commit
# =============================================================================
# Y1.004+: state lives in <repo>/state/ which fs.link maps to a persistent
# drive outside the panel install. Pre-Y1.004 root-level paths are kept
# below so existing installs don't leak files into commits during the
# one-time migration window (state files get moved into state/ on first
# Y1.004 boot — see _migrate_state_dir in mlx_ltx_panel.py).
state
state/
panel_queue.json
panel_hidden.json
panel_settings.json
# 2026-05-31 review: defense-in-depth for the private GitHub-stats data.
# `state/` is an fs.link symlink off-repo, so `git check-ignore
# state/stats-data.jsonl` reports "beyond a symbolic link" — i.e. the only
# thing protecting it today is that it lives outside the repo. A basename
# rule covers it even if PHOSPHENE_STATS_OUT is pointed somewhere tracked,
# or the symlink is ever replaced with a real dir. (A snapshot leaked once
# to docs/stats-data.jsonl — rolled back in 70b4489. Never again.)
**/stats-data.jsonl
stats-data.jsonl
# Same defense-in-depth for the anonymous-usage mirror + the cached fleet
# rollup. These carry no prompts/paths/media by construction, but they are
# still this machine's own telemetry and have no business in a public repo.
**/usage-log.jsonl
usage-log.jsonl
**/usage-fleet.json
usage-fleet.json
*.log
*.tmp
# Manual `.original_<date>` asset backups (e.g. before re-exporting a logo).
# Kept on disk for the author, never committed / shipped (v3.0.7 review P3).
*.original_*

# =============================================================================
# Generated / user content — too big or too personal for git
# =============================================================================
mlx_outputs
mlx_outputs/
panel_uploads
panel_uploads/
audio_inputs
audio_inputs/

# =============================================================================
# Models — ~60 GB, must be downloaded separately (see README)
# =============================================================================
mlx_models
mlx_models/

# =============================================================================
# Third-party — installed alongside, not part of this repo
# =============================================================================
ltx-2-mlx/
# The optional Hailuo H3 pack: install_h3.js clones minimax-h3-mlx INTO the
# app directory (it has to — the panel resolves the runner relative to ROOT,
# and mlx_models/hailuo-h3 is fs.link-mapped from here). It is a separate git
# repo of its own, so to THIS repo it is just a permanently-untracked folder.
# Un-ignored it made `git status --porcelain` never empty, which the panel
# read as "local changes uncommitted" and used to suppress the whole update
# check — every H3 user lost the update pill (#52, @Morac2). Anchored with a
# leading slash: only the clone at the repo root, never a same-named dir
# nested inside a vendored tree.
/minimax-h3-mlx/
.venv/

# =============================================================================
# Pinokio runtime dirs — created next to the app, never ours to commit
# =============================================================================
# ENVIRONMENT points HF_HOME / TORCH_HOME / GRADIO_TEMP_DIR at ./cache/*, and
# install_h3.js passes HF_HOME={{cwd}}/cache/HF_HOME explicitly, so installing
# the H3 pack always leaves content there. `logs/` is the panel's own run log
# dir (*.log alone doesn't cover the directory once it holds anything else).
# Both were only ever invisible to the maintainer because his two clones carry
# them in .git/info/exclude — users never had that, so they hit the same
# permanently-dirty status as the H3 clone above (#52).
/cache/
/logs/

# =============================================================================
# Legacy experimentation files (Comfy workflows, etc.) — not part of the panel
# =============================================================================
civitai_ltxv23_workflow/
ltx23_*.json
ltx_latest_test_view.html
run_ltx_mlx_i2v.sh

# =============================================================================
# Python
# =============================================================================
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/

# =============================================================================
# Local environment / secrets — never commit
# =============================================================================
# .env.local holds Linear API key and any other per-machine secrets used by
# agent tooling (e.g. Linear project sync). Source-of-truth credential file
# is ~/claude/claudio/.env; .env.local just mirrors what this folder needs.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# =============================================================================
# OS / IDE
# =============================================================================
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Claude Preview tool config (per-machine, not Phosphene)
.claude/
